WEBVTT

00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:16,740
I already know that what food allergies I have, and I am mostly gluten, dairy, and sugar-free

00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:24,660
already. What type of diet do you recommend that a phase 2 or phase 3 lime person follow?

00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:31,940
So phase 2 lime is what I have termed people that have chronic lime where

00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:39,940
the bacteria has not gone. The bacteria has gone intracellular, but you haven't formed any

00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:47,220
self-antibody. So you're not in an autoimmune phase. Phase 3 lime is my term for someone who is

00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:53,780
now formed self-antibody because of their lime infection. Now there's other reasons why you can

00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:58,900
develop an autoimmune disease not just because of a bacterial infection,

00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:04,260
Borrelia, or something. There's lots of different things that can trigger an autoimmune

00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:12,020
disease. That means that your system created self-antibodies. But what you have to look for

00:01:12,020 --> 00:01:21,940
with lime disease or if you do have self-antibodies, you have to look for what are my triggers.

00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:30,020
So triggers can change over time. So let's say dietary triggers are one thing and they're

00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:36,100
a very common thing. Maybe the most common thing. But if I'm already dairy-free, I'm already gluten-free

00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:43,060
and I'm already sugar-free, what else do I need to look for? Well, it still can be valuable to run

00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:50,020
a CyRex 10 profile because you may have developed antibodies to things that are in gluten-free foods

00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:55,940
and you don't know it. You might not be noticing any inflammation in the gut. Therefore, you don't

00:01:55,940 --> 00:02:03,860
think that food is causing any issues, but it can be still causing inflammation in the gut,

00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:09,860
not causing symptoms there, but causing symptoms in the brain. Therefore, giving you symptoms with a lot

00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:17,220
what would be known as a lime flare. So if you think you're in phase 2 or phase 3 lime and you're not

00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:25,700
having any problems, your life is going well and you're not experiencing a great deal of symptoms

00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:29,940
or anything. Maybe there isn't anything you need to do. But if you are noticing flares, you're

00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:36,580
noticing symptoms, you need to dig a little bit deeper and see if food is, you've got to look for

00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:42,820
what are called triggers. So anything can be a trigger that is setting off an immune response that's

00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:49,620
setting off a flare. So that can be a food that isn't necessarily causing you any tummy issues. So

00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:56,740
I don't have any issues when I eat corn. So I know it's not it. Well, that's not necessarily true. You

00:02:56,740 --> 00:03:00,740
might not have any stomach issues when you eat corn, but it's causing inflammation in your brain and

00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:07,780
that's causing your lime flare. So it's still valuable if you're having these flares, if you're having

00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:13,860
symptom patterns to do a food sensitivity panel. There's other things that cause flares too. So if

00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:19,540
you're on the autoimmune course, you'll see that there are tons of different things can cause flares,

00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:26,740
not just dietary things. So looking for things that are what are termed triggers that can be

00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:33,140
triggering an immune response and triggering a worsening of your condition is what you really want

00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:34,740
to dig into and look for.

